## Vercel Web Analytics Installation - Completed Successfully

### Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Vite + React project according to the latest official Vercel documentation.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package (version ^2.0.1)
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json` with the new dependency

#### 2. Code Integration
**Modified: `src/App.jsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react'`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the return statement of the main App component
- Component is rendered alongside existing content and BgmToggle components

### Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide for React/Vite projects:
- Documentation source: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Framework: React with Vite build tool
- Integration approach: Added Analytics component to the root App component

The Analytics component will automatically:
- Track page views and web vitals
- Send data to Vercel Analytics dashboard (after deployment)
- Work in both development and production modes
- Handle data collection in a privacy-friendly manner

### Verification Steps Completed

✅ Package successfully installed using npm
✅ Code changes preserve existing functionality
✅ Build process completed successfully (no errors)
✅ Generated production build in dist/ directory (1.21s build time)
✅ All existing components and features remain intact

### Next Steps for User

To complete the setup and start collecting analytics:

1. **Deploy to Vercel**: Push these changes to your repository or deploy directly using `vercel deploy`
2. **Enable Analytics**: In your Vercel dashboard, navigate to your project → Analytics → Enable Web Analytics
3. **Verify Data Collection**: After deployment, check the browser Network tab for `/_vercel/insights/view` requests
4. **View Analytics**: Access your analytics data through the Vercel dashboard under your project's Analytics section

